termin.description:
The temperature should be reached at the selected time. To achieve this, the setpoint is raised in time (never lowered). Up to 4 appointments per type and profile are possible, also several on the same day. All appointments can be changed later in the blueprint.

Entered so far:
{liste}

klima_sender.description:
Choose the IR transmitter **of this room** (e.g. the Broadlink in the living room or the one in the bedroom). PV surplus heating automatically uses the same transmitter.

{grund}

On the next page the integration reads which commands the previous control sent via this transmitter and which are already learned there, and pre-fills everything. Nothing is sent and nothing is learned in the process.

{fehler}

klima.description:
IR transmitter `{sender}`. **Detected:**
{erkennung}

The fields are pre-filled accordingly – usually just check and continue. {stufe} in the command name stands for the temperature (power_{stufe} → power_20), {luefter} for the fan level. Several additional commands are separated by commas and sent one after another, 1 s apart. Missing commands are learned with you in the next step; existing ones are never replaced without your explicit consent.

lernen_test.description:
**{befehl}** ({bedeutung}) {herkunft}.

Test the command with the action `remote.send_command` via `{sender}` and check whether the air conditioner in room **{raum}** responds correctly – this makes sure the command belongs to the right room.

{status}

pv.description:
Sequence: start on surplus with a full battery, close the radiators, the air conditioner heats, heat check, pauses and safety release. All thresholds can be adjusted later in the blueprint.

**Heating commands:** They are sent via the air conditioner's Broadlink (device name `{geraet}`). With {stufe} in the command name there is one command per heating level, e.g. `heizen_22` … `heizen_28`; PV heating sends the selected heating level, which can be changed later without learning again. “Check now” leads directly to learning the missing commands on exactly this Broadlink – each one is then sent once as a test.

{uebernahme}

{heiz_stand}

{fehler}

platz.description:
Layout of view **{ansicht}** (★ = room cards are already here):

{uebersicht}

Choose the section for the card. Recommended sections are listed first and preselected; any other section works as well – including stacks, grids and tabdeck tabs.

position.description:
**{ansicht} › {platz}**

{bild}

Suggested design (detected from the existing cards): **{erkannt}**. The card can be moved later in the dashboard editor or placed again via “Configure”.

altsteuerung.description:
The previous control was found for this Better Thermostat (and the air conditioning transmitter, if any): **{anz_auto} automations**, **{anz_skript} scripts** and **{anz_helfer} helpers**. On creation, the selected automations are switched off, the scripts disabled and both marked with “(alt)” in their name; the selected helpers get “(alt)” in their display name. Nothing is deleted – via “Configure” everything can be switched on again or deleted permanently after a test week.

**Other automations and scripts that use previous helpers of this room** (stay switched on):
{abhaengig}

**Shared with other rooms** (stay unchanged):
{gemeinsam}

{warnungen}

bestaetigen.description:
The following will be created:

**Automations**
{automationen}

**{anzahl} helpers**
{helfer}

**Dashboard card:** {karte}

{hinweise}

The three blueprints are installed if needed. Existing automations, helpers and dashboard cards remain unchanged.

